      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Get Graph Info",
    },
    "description": "Get the connected graph's name and filesystem path.

**Use when:** confirming which graph is attached or debugging paths.
**Can't find:** anything about content. See logseq_list_pages and logseq_build_context.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {},
      "required": [],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_get_graph_info",
    "title": "Get Graph Info",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Get Page",
    },
    "description": "Get a page by name (case-insensitive). With include_children, also its blocks.

**Use when:** you know the page name.
**Can't find:** pages by keyword (logseq_search_blocks, logseq_list_pages) or what links here (logseq_get_backlinks).
**Alternatives:** logseq_build_context adds related pages and references; logseq_get_page_outline for a long page.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "format": {
          "description": "json (default), or markdown text. Markdown has block uuids only on search hits and with compact",
          "enum": [
            "json",
            "markdown",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "include_children": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Whether to include child blocks/pages",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "page_name": {
          "description": "Page name, alias, or ISO date (2025-01-01) for a journal",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "resolve_refs": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Add resolvedContent/resolvedRefs for ((uuid)) refs and {{embed}}s (depth 2)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "page_name",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_get_page",
    "title": "Get Page",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Get Page Outline",
    },
    "description": "List a page's top-level blocks: uuid, the first line (80 characters) and the number of children. Cheaper than logseq_get_page for a long page.

**Use when:** you need a page's shape before reading parts of it. Read the blocks you pick with logseq_get_block.
**Can't find:** nested blocks below the first level, or block text past the first line (logseq_get_block, logseq_get_page).",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "page_name": {
          "description": "Page name, alias, or ISO date (2025-01-01) for a journal",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "page_name",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_get_page_outline",
    "title": "Get Page Outline",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "List Pages",
    },
    "description": "List non-journal page names, filtered by name_contains (substring, not fuzzy).

**Use when:** unsure which pages exist or what the user calls something.
**Can't find:** journals (logseq_query_by_date_range), block text (logseq_search_blocks), or past 200 names (use offset). Warning pages_unavailable: list unknown, not empty.
**Next:** logseq_get_page.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "limit": {
          "default": 200,
          "description": "Max pages (default: 200, max: 1000)",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "name_contains": {
          "description": "Filter page names containing this text (case-insensitive)",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "offset": {
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Pages to skip, in name order; shifts if the graph changes",
          "type": "number",
        },
      },
      "required": [],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_list_pages",
    "title": "List Pages",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Query by Date Range",
    },
    "description": "Query journal entries by date range, last N journals, or named period, with optional search. Give exactly one of: start_date + end_date, last_n, preset.

**Use when:** "what did I do last week?" or catching up. summary.topConcepts shows what a period was about.
**Can't find:** non-journal pages, or days with no journal.
**Alternatives:** logseq_get_concept_evolution, logseq_search_blocks.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "end_date": {
          "description": "End date in YYYYMMDD format (e.g., 20251120). Needs start_date",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "include_content": {
          "default": true,
          "description": "false returns only per-day block counts and top-level snippets",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "last_n": {
          "description": "The N most recent journals that exist (whole number, 1+), newest first",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "preset": {
          "description": "Named period in local time; weeks run Monday to Sunday",
          "enum": [
            "today",
            "yesterday",
            "this_week",
            "last_week",
            "this_month",
            "last_month",
            "this_year",
            "year_to_date",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "resolve_refs": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Add resolvedContent/resolvedRefs for ((uuid)) refs and {{embed}}s (depth 2)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "search_term": {
          "description": "Optional search term to filter blocks",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "slim_results": {
          "default": true,
          "description": "Slim blocks (default). false returns full entities",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "start_date": {
          "description": "Start date in YYYYMMDD format (e.g., 20251115). Needs end_date",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "top_concepts_limit": {
          "default": 10,
          "description": "Entries in summary.topConcepts, the most-linked pages (default 10). 0 omits it",
          "type": "number",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_query_by_date_range",
    "title": "Query by Date Range",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Query by Property",
    },
    "description": "Find blocks whose property equals a value (e.g. status::done).

**Matching:** the key as stored (created-at) or camelCase; values are exact strings ("42", "true"); a multi-value property matches if any one value equals it. Returns a flat list with the page name, no children.
**Can't find:** partial values or ranges. For text use logseq_search_blocks.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "property_key": {
          "description": "Name of the property to query (letters, digits, "-" and "_"; createdAt and created-at are equivalent)",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "property_value": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "type": "number",
            },
            {
              "type": "boolean",
            },
          ],
          "description": "Value to match for the property. For multi-value properties, matches if any one value equals it",
        },
        "slim_results": {
          "default": true,
          "description": "Slim blocks (default). false returns full entities",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "property_key",
        "property_value",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_query_by_property",
    "title": "Query by Property",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Search Blocks",
    },
    "description": "Case-insensitive literal substring search over block content, newest first, capped by limit (max 500). Check hasMore and warnings.

**Can't find:** synonyms, stems or related words (try variants), blocks by property (logseq_query_by_property), link structure (logseq_search_by_relationship), or over 500 matches in one call (narrow the query).
**Next:** logseq_build_context on a result's page.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "include_context": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Include semantic context (page, references, tags)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Maximum number of results to return (default: 100, max: 500)",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "query": {
          "description": "Text to search for in block content",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "slim_results": {
          "default": true,
          "description": "Slim blocks (default). false returns full entities",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "query",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_search_blocks",
    "title": "Search Blocks",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Search by Relationship",
    },
    "description": "Find blocks tied to topic A by a link to topic B: references, referenced-by, in-pages-linking-to, or connected-within N hops. Both topics must be pages.

**Can't find:** relationships that exist only as plain text. Matching is on [[links]] and #tags, not words.
**Alternatives:** logseq_search_blocks (keywords), logseq_get_concept_network (overview).",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "max_distance": {
          "default": 2,
          "description": "Maximum graph distance for connected-within (default: 2)",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "relationship_type": {
          "description": "Type of relationship: references (blocks about A that reference B), referenced-by (blocks about A in pages referenced by B), in-pages-linking-to (blocks about A in pages linking to B), connected-within (topics connected within N hops)",
          "enum": [
            "references",
            "referenced-by",
            "in-pages-linking-to",
            "connected-within",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "topic_a": {
          "description": "Primary topic to search for (page name, alias or ISO date)",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "topic_b": {
          "description": "Related topic that defines the relationship (page name, alias or ISO date)",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "topic_a",
        "topic_b",
        "relationship_type",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_search_by_relationship",
    "title": "Search by Relationship",
  },
]
